  "domain": "infer-core",
  "level": "L2",
  "title": "Tokenizer admission, generation reservation and image limits bound different resources",
  "mechanism": "TGI validation sends requests through unbounded channels to blocking tokenizer workers; the Python tokenizer uses one worker. prepare_input encodes the full rewritten input before the retained token suffix and accounting are truncated. The current generation pass reserves at most DEFAULT_GENERATION_LENGTH while retaining a separate total-new-token request. HTTP image loading bounds encoded response bytes; the data-URI branch has no max_image_fetch_size check in this function.",
  "corrections": [
    "Do not claim the fetch byte cap is a decoded image-memory cap. Image-library default limits were not inspected.",
    "The zero-worker constructor path can spin, but v2 CLI main.rs:147-150 rejects zero validation_workers; do not report this as a demonstrated deployed configuration bug.",
    "Vertex join_all waits for all sibling futures before collecting the Result; a returned error does not make it cancel siblings.",
    "Vertex maps errors returned from generate_internal to 500, but this unit does not establish every upstream validation-error path.",
    "The caller's dropped reply does not cancel work already running in the blocking worker."
  ],
  "source_scope": "All 22 corrected reference ranges read; library decoding defaults and production concurrency were not executed.",
